      },
      "text": "By virtue of the authority vested in \nme by Articles 36 and 56 of the Uniform \nCode of Military Justice (established by \nthe act of May 5,1950, 64 Stat. 107), and \nas President of the United States, it is \nordered that the Manual for Courts- \nMartial, United States, 1951 (prescribed \nby Executive Order No. 10214 of Febru­\nary 8,1951), be, and it is hereby, amend­\ned as follows:"
    },
    {
      "char_end": 2131,
      "char_start": 1722,
      "id": "CLAUSES:EO:10565#1",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "1.",
      "pdf_page": 3,
      "scope_id": "EO:10565#1",
      "source": {
        "filing_date": null,
        "location_confidence": "high",
        "location_verified": false,
        "page_or_item": "19 FR 6299, PDF pages 3-3",
        "requires_page_check": false,
        "sha256": "488ba616bbf77e917165f795ae8fcf2a980ca5a0cc5b047ac1373185ad7767ff",
        "signing_date": "1954-09-28",
        "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_10565.txt",
        "text_sha256": "23d112863ce3be074e3ed9b39e4781ce892832ef55df09709e8aa0390ec81e2a",
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1954-09-30/pdf/FR-1954-09-30.pdf"
      },
      "text": "1. The following language is added to \nsubparagraph 76a (6) at the end thereof: \n“If an accused is found guilty of an \noffense or offenses for none of which dis­\nhonorable discharge is authorized, proof \nof three or more previous convictions \nduring the year next preceding the com­\nmission of any offense of which the ac­\ncused stands convicted will authorize dis­\nhonorable discharge. See 127c, Section \nB.”"
    },
    {
      "char_end": 2249,
      "char_start": 2132,
      "id": "CLAUSES:EO:10565#2",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "2.",
      "pdf_page": 3,
      "scope_id": "EO:10565#2",
      "source": {
        "filing_date": null,
        "location_confidence": "high",
        "location_verified": false,
        "page_or_item": "19 FR 6299, PDF pages 3-3",
        "requires_page_check": false,
        "sha256": "488ba616bbf77e917165f795ae8fcf2a980ca5a0cc5b047ac1373185ad7767ff",
        "signing_date": "1954-09-28",
        "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_10565.txt",
        "text_sha256": "23d112863ce3be074e3ed9b39e4781ce892832ef55df09709e8aa0390ec81e2a",
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1954-09-30/pdf/FR-1954-09-30.pdf"
      },
      "text": "2. The offenses and punishments listed \nin the Table of Maximum Punishments, \ncontained in paragraph 127c, for viola-"
    },
    {
      "char_end": 3301,
      "char_start": 2250,
      "id": "CLAUSES:EO:10565#3",
      "kind": "amendment_instruction",
      "label": "3.",
      "pdf_page": 3,
      "scope_id": "EO:10565#3",
      "source": {
        "filing_date": null,
        "location_confidence": "high",
        "location_verified": false,
        "page_or_item": "19 FR 6299, PDF pages 3-3",
        "requires_page_check": false,
        "sha256": "488ba616bbf77e917165f795ae8fcf2a980ca5a0cc5b047ac1373185ad7767ff",
        "signing_date": "1954-09-28",
        "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_10565.txt",
        "text_sha256": "23d112863ce3be074e3ed9b39e4781ce892832ef55df09709e8aa0390ec81e2a",
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1954-09-30/pdf/FR-1954-09-30.pdf"
      },
      "text": "3. Section B, Permissible Additional  \nPunishments,  of paragraph 127c is \namended by adding thereto at the be­\nginning thereof the following language: \n“If an accused is found guilty of an \noffense or offenses for none of which dis­\nhonorable discharge is authorized, proof \nof three or more previous convictions \nduring the year next preceding the \ncommission of any offense of which the \naccused stands convicted will authorize \ndishonorable discharge and forfeiture of \nall pay and allowances and, if the con­\nfinement otherwise authorized is less \nthan one year, confinement at hard labor\ntions of Articles 86 and 87 of the Uni­\nform Code of Military Justice are revised \nso that they shall be as follows:\nfor one year. In computing the one- \nyear period preceding the commission \nof any offense, periods of unauthorized \n\"absence as shown by the findings in the \ncase or by the evidence of previous con­\nvictions should be excluded. See 75 b (2) \nas to further limitations concerning evi­\ndence of previous convictions which may \nbe considered.”"
    }
  ],
